# vendor/ is no longer committed, as of the move to a public GitHub repo.
#
# It used to be, deliberately, so the plugin could deploy without a composer
# install. That reasoning was sound while the repo was private on Bitbucket. It
# stops being sound in a public repo: it publishes a vendored copy of
# PhpSpreadsheet and its dependencies, ~675 files, and pins the studio to
# whatever versions happened to be on Jason's Mac.
#
# What replaces it: .github/workflows/release.yml runs `composer install
# --no-dev` and builds the zip, so the RELEASE still contains vendor/ exactly as
# before. Nothing changes for the sites receiving it.
#
# The catch, and it matters because there is no composer on the studio Mac: a
# fresh clone of this repo will have no vendor/, and the plugin will fatal until
# one exists. Either install composer locally (see docs/DEPLOY.md) or download a
# built zip from the Releases page and copy its vendor/ across.
vendor/
.claude/
.phpunit.cache/
.phpunit.result.cache

